       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that ceiling. A dose this high raises the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI bleeding, and hyponatremia, and it has no proven added benefit.\n\nCould this be a typo or a unit mix-up? Here are some options:\n\n- **Standard titration:** start at 50 mg once daily, or 25 mg for anxiety or panic disorder. Increase in 25\u201350 mg steps at intervals of at least one week, up to 200 mg/day.\n- **200 mg once daily:** I can enter this right away if you want the maximum dose.\n- **400 mg is intended:** tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording your rationale, for example a documented specialist recommendation or a plan for monitoring. Pharmacy will probably still want to verify it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
